This work examines an elliptic system defined by
\begin{align*}
\begin{cases}
-\Delta u_i=\lambda_i f_i(u_i), & \text{in } \Omega, \\
u_i=0, & \text{on } \partial\Omega,
\end{cases}
\end{align*}
where $\Omega \subset \mathbb{R}^N$ is a bounded domain with $N \geq 3$. The functions $f_i$ are continuous, bounded, and possess the sign condition, while the parameter set is given by $\{\lambda_i\}_{i=1}^k$. Our analysis establishes that for sufficiently large $\lambda_i$, the system admits a positive solution. Furthermore, we demonstrate the existence of a continuum of solutions when $\{\lambda_i\}_{i=1}^k$ are sufficiently large.

